Take rules_cuda from the teaspan fork

ccv_deps() is what declares @build_bazel_rules_cuda, so this is where a
consumer has to redirect it. The fork carries two patches. One lets
TF_CUDA_COMPUTE_CAPABILITIES hold a three-digit capability, which the pinned
validator rejects outright, and without which no Blackwell arch can be built.
The other keys nvcc's --keep directory off the output object, fixing a
pre-existing race between the PIC and non-PIC compiles of a source that every
added -gencode makes likelier.

The branch is liuliu's pin plus those two commits, so the merge-base is still
the commit ccv named here. See patches/rules_cuda/README.md.
